        fix: b"Convert explicitly: `f32(x)`, `u32(x)`, `i32(x)`; write a literal of the right \
            type: `1u`, `1i`, `1.0`.",
        example: b"embed wgsl K {\n\
            \x20   @compute @workgroup_size(1)\n\
            \x20   fn main() {\n\
            \x20       let v = vec3<f32>(1.0);\n\
            \x20       let w = v + 2i;\n\
            \x20   }\n\
            }\n\
            \n\
            main.vl:5:19: error[wgsl.type] '+' cannot take vec3<f32> and i32\n\
            \x20 help: convert one side: f32(...)",
    },
    Explain {
        code: b"wgsl.redefined",
        severity: b"error",
        means: b"A name declared twice in the same scope (module scope, a struct's members, a \
